INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES
  ('how-online-ordering-is-enhancing-customer-satisfaction-and-loyalty', 'How Online Ordering is Enhancing Customer Satisfaction and Loyalty', 'Hey there! Have you noticed how the way we order food has changed so dramatically in recent years? Think about it, just a few years ago, the idea of food ordering apps might have seemed like a novelty rather than a...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Hey there! Have you noticed how the way we order food has changed so dramatically in recent years? Think about it, just a few years ago, the idea of food ordering apps might have seemed like a novelty rather than a necessity. Fast forward to today, and online ordering has become an integral part of our daily lives, especially for those of us who love the convenience it brings. But have you ever wondered how this shift towards online ordering is enhancing customer satisfaction and loyalty? Let''s dig into it!"},{"type":"h2","text":"The Convenience Factor Online Ordering"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the most obvious yet impactful ways online ordering has transformed the dining landscape is through sheer convenience. With just a few clicks or taps, you can have your favorite meal delivered right to your doorstep or ready for pick-up. The days of waiting on hold to place a phone order or driving across town only to find out your favorite dish is sold out are long gone."},{"type":"h2","text":"24/7 Availability"},{"type":"p","text":"For those of us who have irregular schedules or late-night cravings, online ordering systems often operate around the clock. You can place orders whenever it''s most convenient for you, rather than being restricted by the restaurant’s phone hours. This 24/7 availability means that you can satisfy your cravings anytime, contributing to higher customer satisfaction."},{"type":"h2","text":"Streamlined Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Imagine never having to repeat your order three times over a noisy phone line or getting stuck in a miscommunication loop. Online menus are clear and detailed, making it simpler to customize orders to fit your unique preferences and dietary needs. The ease of use significantly cuts down on mistakes, leading to higher satisfaction rates."},{"type":"h2","text":"Personalization and Customization"},{"type":"p","text":"Another exciting advantage of online ordering is the level of personalization it offers. From saved favorite orders to personalized recommendations based on past orders, online platforms can tailor the experience to individual tastes. When customers feel understood and catered to, it naturally fosters loyalty."},{"type":"h2","text":"User Profiles"},{"type":"p","text":"Many online ordering systems allow users to create profiles where their preferences, past orders, and payment information are stored for quick and easy reordering. This not only saves time but also enhances the overall customer experience by making it more personal and convenient."},{"type":"h2","text":"Special Offers and Discounts"},{"type":"p","text":"Promotions tailored to individual buying habits can be directly communicated through online platforms. Whether it’s a discount on a frequently ordered item or a special offer on a customer’s birthday, personalized perks encourage repeat business and enhance customer loyalty."},{"type":"h2","text":"Speed and Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"Let’s be honest: nobody likes waiting. One of the worst parts of traditional ordering methods is the waiting time, whether it''s being on hold over the phone or waiting in line at the restaurant. Online ordering drastically reduces these waiting times by streamlining the entire process."},{"type":"h2","text":"Real-Time Order Tracking"},{"type":"p","text":"Ever wondered exactly when your food will arrive? Many online ordering systems offer real-time order tracking, allowing customers to monitor their order''s progress from preparation to delivery. The transparency reassures customers and adds to their overall satisfaction."},{"type":"h2","text":"Faster Service"},{"type":"p","text":"Since the ordering process is digital, the time taken for a staff member to take and relay your order is minimized. This means food gets prepared faster, drivers can pick it up quicker, and you, the customer, get to enjoy your meal sooner."},{"type":"h2","text":"Contactless and Safe Transactions"},{"type":"p","text":"In the age of a global pandemic, health and safety have never been more paramount. Online ordering systems offer contactless payment and delivery options, which significantly contribute to customer satisfaction."},{"type":"h2","text":"Multiple Payment Options"},{"type":"p","text":"From credit cards to mobile wallets, online platforms offer various payment methods, making transactions quicker and safer. Contactless payment options reduce the need for physical interaction, ensuring customer safety and peace of mind."},{"type":"h2","text":"Contactless Delivery"},{"type":"p","text":"Customers can opt for contactless delivery, where the food can be left at a specified location, reducing person-to-person contact. This added layer of safety has made online ordering particularly appealing during these uncertain times."},{"type":"h2","text":"Building Loyalty through Rewards Programs"},{"type":"p","text":"Loyalty programs are often seamlessly integrated into online ordering platforms. Every order placed could earn points, discounts, or other rewards, encouraging customers to keep coming back."},{"type":"h2","text":"Easy Enrollment and Redemption"},{"type":"p","text":"Gone are the days of carrying around physical loyalty cards. With online ordering, loyalty programs are often just a tap away. Points can be automatically added to your profile and easily redeemed during future orders, significantly enhancing the customer experience."},{"type":"h2","text":"Engagement through Feedback"},{"type":"p","text":"Online ordering systems make it easy to collect feedback immediately after order completion. This real-time feedback loop allows restaurants to quickly address any issues, thereby improving service and fostering customer loyalty."},{"type":"h2","text":"Ready for a Better Dining Experience?"},{"type":"p","text":"So, there you have it! Online ordering is not just a fleeting trend but a transformative shift in how we engage with restaurants. It''s making our lives more convenient, our food experiences more personalized, and our interactions safer, all while building stronger bonds of loyalty. If you haven’t embraced online ordering yet, maybe it’s time to give it a try and see how it can enhance your dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Ready to see how your favorite restaurant fares with online ordering? Dive into the future of dining and place your first online order today! You might just find that it''s a game-changer for your culinary adventures. Happy ordering!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_709240d8e6ce4d3baab116a7ea0b19c3~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2025-05-16', 'published'),
  ('how-to-make-your-staff-measurably-happy', 'How to Make Your Staff Measurably Happy', 'For the champions (staff) who keep our industry running, restaurant work requires long hours, atypical schedules, and a few days off. The grind is real and impacts the health, financial stability, and satisfaction of...', '[{"type":"p","text":"For the champions (staff) who keep our industry running, restaurant work requires long hours, atypical schedules, and a few days off. The grind is real and impacts the health, financial stability, and satisfaction of all types of restaurant employees, no matter their role or tenure."},{"type":"p","text":"Feedback from restaurant workers indicates low overall employee happiness compared with other industries, leaving restaurateurs with the task of confronting employee turnover by analyzing standards of workplace happiness and coming up with solutions to make the hospitality industry hospitable for its workers."},{"type":"h2","text":"What is Workplace Happiness?"},{"type":"p","text":"Several factors influence workplace happiness, including those needed for daily motivation (like wages, bonuses, and benefits) and others that result in long-term satisfaction (like financial stability, stress, health, and growth opportunities). But workplace happiness in the restaurant the industry is unique."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants face high employee turnover, with data from a Bureau of Labor Statistics program reflecting a 74.9% turnover rate at restaurants in 2018, elevated from 72.5% in 2017. This number far outpaces the average rate in private sector jobs, estimated at 48.9% for 2018."},{"type":"p","text":"Staff employed in restaurants, pubs, bars, cafes, or catering might turn over quickly due to demographics. Moreover, restaurants use high numbers of teenagers, students, and seasonal staffers , and the cost of turnover cost per employee can reach thousands of dollars regarding training, onboarding, and, ultimately, productivity loss."},{"type":"p","text":"This cycle becomes a self-fulfilling prophecy, where employers avoid investing in employees, believing they will leave within two to three months."},{"type":"p","text":"Josh said the goal is to find what employees need to be happy. \"If you''re working toward that in a healthy way and with support, happiness is what happens, and happiness is nice, but it doesn''t support itself without having a reason for being.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Suppose you take the student workers out of the equation. In that case, the restaurant employee turnover remains bleak at best, with hospitality workers reporting lower happiness than those in other industries."},{"type":"p","text":"At eatOS, we look into ways of measuring workplace happiness, along with tested and evolving technologies for making each task easy and accurate. As they say, happy workers are the most productive ones. And once you perform well in your workplace, restaurant happiness occurs."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_53f922a91cb34404ac76b51486e80ad2~mv2.jpg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2025-05-15', 'published'),
  ('how-to-photograph-food-perfectly', 'How to photograph food perfectly?', 'Christmas is already around the corner. People are now busy shopping, buying Christmas presence and dining at their favorite restaurants. Today more than ever is the perfect time to improve your menu boards, flyers and...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Christmas is already around the corner. People are now busy shopping, buying Christmas presence and dining at their favorite restaurants. Today more than ever is the perfect time to improve your menu boards, flyers and brochures."},{"type":"p","text":"Some business indeed depends on advertising company to manage their promotional materials. However, a lot of small businesses are doing it their way."},{"type":"p","text":"If you have ever tried to take a picture of your meal for Instagram, you know that beautiful food photography is more challenging than it looks and yet it is crucial for restaurants and food businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"According to studies, including pictures on your online menu can help you increase sales by as much as 30%. eatOS prepares five food photography tricks that will help you show off your hard work in the best light:"},{"type":"h2","text":"Think and create a story you want to tell"},{"type":"p","text":"A food picture should be able to help you tell your business''s story and brand. Think about what kind of atmosphere you want to showcase and what the best features of the food and restaurant are. An overhead shot of a crowded table might be best if your brand is about abundance. If you are all about comfort food, try a close-up of a juicy burger or a cheesy one. Creative planning can improve your photos immensely."},{"type":"h2","text":"Plate beautifully and style the scene"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not be afraid to get creative with your food photography. Of course, you have got to work with the materials you have so your photos accurately represent the experience customers will have when they come in. But make sure you style the scene carefully, adding or subtracting napkins, glassware, condiments, and other ''props'' to create the best image and take care with your plating, arrange the food to showcase natural colors and make a full plate."},{"type":"p","text":"Use a salad plate if necessary to avoid having too much empty plate space, and let your artistic side out when you add that little dollop of sauce just so."},{"type":"h2","text":"Make sure to provide proper lighting."},{"type":"p","text":"Natural light is always best, but do not put your food in direct sunlight-and never use a flash. The light from direct sunlight will be too harsh and the shadows too deep-and a flash will wash out the colors in your image. Instead, aim for bright but indirect, natural light. The real pros will use a bounce board to direct the light where they want it and fill in shadows. If you are not getting the look you want, you can try many cheap and DIY options."},{"type":"h2","text":"Consider Composition"},{"type":"p","text":"Here is another pro tip: great photographers often use the \"rule of thirds\" to compose their images. If you imagine your image is divided into a 3×3 grid, you are trying to align your image''s primary focus with the grid''s lines and intersections and placing your subject to one side or the other of the image, using that grid, can often create a more dynamic-feeling image."},{"type":"p","text":"If you are using a smartphone, check your camera app settings, most have the option to overlay a grid while you are shooting to help you think about your composition."},{"type":"h2","text":"Experiment"},{"type":"p","text":"Great photographers do not just walk into a photo shoot, take one perfect shot, and then walk away. They take hundreds of pictures from many angles and choose the best two or three to use. Do not be afraid to experiment, shoot the same dish from above and from the side, shoot multiple dishes together and one showstopper item alone, or add a prop or a garnish if the image feels flat. Excellent food photography, like anything else, takes practice."},{"type":"p","text":"After taking great pictures for your menu, you must incorporate Self Service kiosk and the right POS system for your business. A great way to reduce labor costs, minimize waiting times and increase profitability. Easy to use and manage, it seamlessly integrates with the point of sale and kitchen display system."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_8c0dd0c7da5147c892698e50eca2ac92~mv2.jpg', 'Marketing & Loyalty', 'eatOS Staff', '2025-05-13', 'published'),
  ('how-to-raise-your-prices-successfully', 'How to Raise Your Prices Successfully', 'The pandemic is why all businesses were forced to re-consider almost everything, from operations to staffing to customer experience. It’s been an enormous challenge, and many companies have lost revenue they couldn’t...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The pandemic is why all businesses were forced to re-consider almost everything, from operations to staffing to customer experience. It’s been an enormous challenge, and many companies have lost revenue they couldn’t afford to lose."},{"type":"p","text":"But when the situation becomes more challenging, it is also a perfect opportunity to reexamine aspects of your business. First, review some policies that might have yet to be questioned. For example, perhaps you’ve been rethinking your tipping approach as more and more customers are doing pickup or takeout. Apart from that, there is a big possibility that you have negotiated some supplier agreements or streamlined other costs."},{"type":"p","text":"Moreover, the tail end of the coronavirus pandemic is the worst possible time to raise prices. Business needs to survive; if you’ve looked at your books and you need to increase your costs, there are ways to implement it without hurting your customers badly."},{"type":"h2","text":"Here are seven strategies for successfully increasing your prices."},{"type":"h2","text":"1\\. Plan ahead"},{"type":"p","text":"It’s difficult to predict what’s coming in the next few years, considering all the uncertainty around the course of the pandemic. But it’s best not to raise prices twice in a short period. Instead, it is recommended to make a plan to get you through a worst-case scenario year in which labor and supply costs continue to rise, but consumers pull back on spending. Then, always remember to set your new prices at a level that will keep your business healthy for a year of uncertainty."},{"type":"h2","text":"2\\. Study your competitors"},{"type":"p","text":"Consider yourself a customer and research what other businesses in your area are up to. Think outside the box when it comes to considering your competitors. Are there independent stylists making house calls in your area who might lure customers from your salon? Could your customers get a meal-kit subscription as an alternative to takeout from your restaurant? Look at what all these competitors are doing on pricing, other local businesses may be raising prices, and many national chains are, too."},{"type":"h2","text":"3\\. Prepare your staff"},{"type":"p","text":"It would be best if you prepared your staff to handle questions about the price increase. You need to post a message on your social media accounts or your website, so it would be perfect if you talked to them and asked them to answer it accordingly. Moreover, you can give them talking points when customers bring up the issue. You may take a few minutes before each shift for a week or two to roleplay a conversation about the prices, so they should be prepared to answer in a friendly, upbeat way. And make sure you prepare your staff for the likelihood that a few customers will be angry and may even threaten to take their business elsewhere. Remind them of the usual best practices for handling difficult customer conversations."},{"type":"h2","text":"4\\. Look for creative alternatives"},{"type":"p","text":"During the early phases of the pandemic, some small businesses added temporary surcharges to cover new expenses like increased staff time spent cleaning or the cost of personal protective equipment. In addition, some restaurants added service charges to ensure staff was fairly compensated while customers were doing more delivery and takeout."},{"type":"p","text":"If you’re facing sharp price increases for certain supplies, look for ways you could avoid using that particular product or look to add a temporary surcharge to specific items. For example, beef, chicken, and pork prices are up about 10%, and many small restaurants are pulling pricier meats off the menu in response."},{"type":"p","text":"However, be aware that communication is key, a sudden new charge can backfire if perceived as opportunistic. Make sure new costs are clearly explained on your website, with signage in your store, and through staff communication with customers."},{"type":"h2","text":"5\\. Don’t just raise prices. Revamp your offerings"},{"type":"p","text":"A service business might add new, higher-touch packages with a higher price tag and some discounted packages for price-sensitive customers. A restaurant might introduce price increases along with a newly refreshed seasonal menu. If customers see that they have options and that you’re making an effort to keep your business up to date with changing trends, they’ll more readily accept a price increase. It is crucial to know that while it’s essential to be transparent about price increases and communicate with customers. Price increases may be easier to accept if they come with a fully upgraded menu of offerings."},{"type":"h2","text":"6\\. Make sure your customer service is a top-notch"},{"type":"p","text":"It is best to ensure you’ll offer your patrons great value considering your new, higher price points. Excellent customer service can help smooth over any problems that may come from higher prices and make your customers feel like they are getting great value for a modestly higher price. Look for cheap ways to create a premium experience through customer service or design elements that enhance your brand."},{"type":"h2","text":"7\\. Plan to revisit the pricing issue in six months"},{"type":"p","text":"No business doesn’t impose price increases, whether there is a pandemic, inflation, economic crisis, or product shortage. Therefore, it is even more crucial to keep checking your business key indicators and monitor how well your current price points are serving you. Always consider planning for the worst-case scenario and ways to keep your business strong. Then, keep checking in and reevaluating whether your prices are too high to maintain your margins."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_9d35c9bc12914a66a40c109a3fdf3d3d~mv2.jpg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2025-05-09', 'published'),
  ('how-to-start-a-food-stand', 'How to start a food stand?', 'It is expected that opening a traditional restaurant can carry a lot of risks. Once you choose a location, you are locked in - potentially for years, depending on your lease agreement. Apart from that, you will likely...', '[{"type":"p","text":"It is expected that opening a traditional restaurant can carry a lot of risks. Once you choose a location, you are locked in - potentially for years, depending on your lease agreement. Apart from that, you will likely spend much more money for rent, utilities, and other expenses from operating at a bricks-and-mortar location."},{"type":"p","text":"On the other hand, food stands and trucks are mobile which can relocate to the hottest spots at any moment. The startup costs are also considerably lower, with the vehicle often being the largest expense."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, you can set up shop anywhere. Major urban centers with high-volume foot traffic tend to be the most lucrative, with some food carts generating $3,000-plus daily."},{"type":"p","text":"However, do not discount county fairs and other travelling venues, which generate heavy demand for hot dogs, ice cream, burritos, funnel cakes, tacos, smoothies, and other delicious treats you could conceivably sell from a mobile food business."},{"type":"p","text":"Many traditional restaurants also invest in dedicated food stands to expand their reach. Going mobile allows them to set up pop-up shops or attend local festivals."},{"type":"p","text":"For more reasons to launch a career in this field, read our guide on the benefits of starting a food truck business. This article discusses opening a food stand and taking payments from your customers."},{"type":"h2","text":"How to start a food stand business?"},{"type":"p","text":"Every jurisdiction is slightly different. Thus, the exact steps for launching a food stand vary depending on the geographic area you plan to serve. Below are some of the most general aspects you will need to consider when setting up your food stand."},{"type":"h2","text":"Know your target market"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most essential starting step for all businesses. A target customer determines what, where, and how much of whatever you sell. There must be a ready market for your culinary creations for your business to grow and succeed. For tips on how to create customer personas, be sure to read our article here."},{"type":"h2","text":"Study the competition"},{"type":"p","text":"When starting a food stand business, you must check out the local competition. This means tracking the locations of other mobile food stands. It also means being aware of bricks-and-mortar eating establishments within walking distance of every place you plan to sell food."},{"type":"p","text":"There is no rule preventing two taco stands from operating on the same block, but it is essential to understand what you are up against before committing any resources."},{"type":"h2","text":"Outsource financing"},{"type":"p","text":"Starting a food stand can cost anywhere from a few thousand dollars to several tens of thousands of dollars. It all depends on the type of equipment you will need and whether you will be renting a stand, purchasing a pre-built structure, or buying into a franchise. Local permitting and food stand requirements can also affect startup costs."},{"type":"p","text":"If you can finance everything out of pocket, that will help you start on the right foot without any debt. Otherwise, you may need funding from investors, banks, friends, and family members. Either way, developing a business plan is essential. Be sure to check out our small business resource page for more tips on starting a new venture."},{"type":"h2","text":"Register your food stand business"},{"type":"p","text":"The next step involves choosing a legal structure for your business."},{"type":"ul","items":["Sole proprietorships are common among solo entrepreneurs due to the low startup and maintenance costs. However, with this legal structure, your personal and business assets become intertwined."]},{"type":"ul","items":["Partnerships make sense if two or more owners are involved with the business."]},{"type":"ul","items":["Due to this structure''s legal protections, many prominent and established companies favor corporations."]},{"type":"ul","items":["Limited liability companies (LLCs) offer a good balance of setup effort and legal protection."]},{"type":"h2","text":"Source equipment"},{"type":"p","text":"The type of food stands you launch and what equipment and supplies you will need."},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"ul","items":["There may only be a need of displays, tables, shelves, and a vehicle to transport these items if selling canned goods."]},{"type":"p","text":"If cooking meals or keeping inventory cold, you will need a lot more equipment - e.g., stoves, freezers, and gas canisters. These extra items may also increase your permitting and licensing costs (covered in the next section)."},{"type":"h2","text":"Obtain permitting and licensing"},{"type":"p","text":"Most municipalities require that food stands secure proper permitting before they operate. Contact your local city hall to find out what requirements apply to your business. It is possible that you may need to go through a separate permitting process with each jurisdiction to serve different geographic areas."},{"type":"h2","text":"Start taking payments"},{"type":"p","text":"Although it is possible to sustain a cash-only food stand business, the pandemic has encouraged many businesses to accept card-based and contactless mobile payment options that do not involve a direct exchange between merchants and customers."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS offers a range of point-of-sale (POS) solutions for food stands. Our full-featured countertop POS terminals can handle even the most complex payment tasks - including barcode scanning and receipt printing."},{"type":"p","text":"To quickly accept payments in the field, we recommend the eatOS payment system that can securely process credit, debit, and contactless payments wherever your food stand business takes you."},{"type":"p","text":"Launching a business is not easy, but with the tips above, you now have the information you need to go from idea creation to your first hungry customer. When you are ready to start making sales, keep eatOS in mind. Our POS solutions helps you in taking payments and running your business easier. To request a free demo of our POS solutions, contact us today."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_c7eff76e25c54afaa7dd748356228f17~mv2.jpg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2025-05-07', 'published'),
  ('identify-the-ideal-workforce-management-company-for-your-business-with-this-comprehensive-guide', 'Workforce Management Company for Your Business', 'For businesses managing many employees, it can be challenging to ensure efficient workforce organization. The right workforce management company can provide various employment solutions, including payroll processing and...', '[{"type":"p","text":"For businesses managing many employees, it can be challenging to ensure efficient workforce organization. The right workforce management company can provide various employment solutions, including payroll processing and time-tracking services. With the help of such services, companies can easily manage their employees'' hours, ensure accurate billing, reduce overtime costs, and improve compliance. However, choosing the perfect workforce management service for your business is no small task. There are a plethora of companies offering numerous benefits, and each claim to be the best. To make your decision easier, here is a comprehensive guide to help you choose the right workforce management company for your business."},{"type":"h2","text":"What is workforce management and its importance to businesses?"},{"type":"p","text":"Workforce management is a crucial tool for businesses of all sizes. It involves technology to optimize employee utilization and performance, helping create a more efficient workforce to deliver better results. Businesses can track employee attendance, manage payroll and other costs, and maximize productivity using a workforce management system. With the right tools and strategy, your business can achieve its goals more quickly and efficiently. With this powerful tool, you can reduce labor costs, improve customer service, and increase profits. Investing in workforce management solutions can help you up your game in the competition and ensure your business remains profitable."},{"type":"h2","text":"How to choose the right workforce management company for your business?"},{"type":"p","text":"Selecting the right workforce management company for your business is a crucial decision that can make or break the success of your organization. Many companies offer workforce management services and choosing the wrong one can be costly. There are a few points to consider which can help you make the best decision for your business."},{"type":"p","text":"First, evaluate their experience. How long has the company been in business? Do they specialize in specific industries or markets? What kind of expertise do they have? It holds paramount importance that you must make sure they have the targeted knowledge and skillset to help your business operate more efficiently."},{"type":"p","text":"Second, research their record of accomplishment. What have other customers said? Have any partnerships with well-known customers ever been announced? Finding out as much as possible about the organization before entering a relationship can give you a bird''s eye view of their future engagement in your business."},{"type":"p","text":"Finally, ask questions! Speak to workforce management company members and understand how they operate and whether their solutions are suitable for your business. It is important for you to feel confident that you are making the right choice when choosing your workforce management partner."},{"type":"h2","text":"What type of workforce management services do you need?"},{"type":"p","text":"Maintaining a successful workforce requires careful planning, organization, and monitoring. From staffing and budgeting to knowledge management, companies must ensure their employees are ready for any challenge and can meet the job''s demands. Workforce management services provide employers with the necessary tools and resources to help them navigate the complexities of managing their staff. Companies can develop a more effective, efficient, and profitable workplace by using employee scheduling software, tracking attendance, managing benefits and rewards programs, establishing performance metrics and goals, and understanding legal requirements. Not only that, but they will be able to retain their most valuable asset: their employees."},{"type":"h2","text":"Determine the size of the workforce management company you need."},{"type":"p","text":"Whether a small business or an international corporation, having the right workforce management company can impact your overall success. But what size of management company do you need for your business can be an important question. To answer that question, start by considering your organization''s goals and evaluating the current size of your workforce. If you have a large team that is geographically dispersed or in multiple locations, you will need a larger company to manage it effectively. Additionally, if you plan to scale up quickly, you may need a larger company with more resources to handle the growth. Ultimately, determining the size of the workforce management company that you need is about understanding your needs and finding the best partner to help you achieve them."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion:"},{"type":"p","text":"Choosing the right workforce management company can improve operational efficiency and employee compliance, leading to better business outcomes. Companies should research their options carefully, making sure that the provider meets their specific requirements and can offer a comprehensive solution. With reliable data and insights into labor costs, companies can make well-informed decisions that lead to successful workforce strategies to give them a competitive edge for their business."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_efe4b72dcac34e42b1cf928c2103440b~mv2.jpg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2025-05-02', 'published'),
  ('instagram-for-restaurant-a-brief-marketing-guide', 'Instagram for Restaurant: A brief marketing guide', 'It has been proven that social media is the most effective laurel for promoting any business. Apart from that, it is no secret that it is a prominent aspect of our daily lives. A study shows that we spend 15% of our...', '[{"type":"p","text":"It has been proven that social media is the most effective laurel for promoting any business. Apart from that, it is no secret that it is a prominent aspect of our daily lives. A study shows that we spend 15% of our lives scrolling through social media.Restaurant owners can reach a broad audience with a well-planned and professional presence on all social media channels and platforms, specifically Instagram, which is in the top-five most used platforms. Below are some crucial insights about Instagram, which we researched to share with you. Instagram Basics for Restaurant Marketing Instagram''s advertising scope grew 12.8 per cent over the past year and now reaches roughly 1 billion monthly users. What started as a photo-sharing platform has become one of the most used apps daily because of its ease of use, accessibility, and overall experience it creates for users."},{"type":"p","text":"Instagram is necessary for any restaurant wanting to entice guests to its establishment. Most of their features are free, so you don''t have to drop much cash into your advertising budget. Post and display your best images"},{"type":"p","text":"Instagram followers look for eye-catching photos. To keep people from scrolling past your posts, displaying dynamic pictures is essential. You want to capture the delectable essence of your plates, so make sure you take professional-looking pics highlighting the beauty of your composed dishes.Are you a novice photographer? Don''t worry! Instagram offers a variety of filters to enhance lighting. There are also editing tools to help craft beautiful posts. Instagram also recommends the following to catch followers'' attention:· Fill the frame: Posting pics that take up the whole frame tends to stand out more. Also, consider a vertical orientation.· Play aroundwith video and reel techniques: Add some pizzazzto your reelswith fun bordersto animated elements."},{"type":"h2","text":"Shout out to Food Holidays"},{"type":"p","text":"Food holidays are a fun way to celebrate culinary culture and connect with followers. Highlighting these special times throughout the year is a great way to drive engagement and seasonal offerings at your restaurant. Create a calendar of exciting or relevant food days and post content with the corresponding hashtag."},{"type":"p","text":"If you have a social media manager, she/he must be aware of the pros and cons of using social media in marketing your business. It is crucial to keep your presence high and your engagement with your target market. It is easier and more accurate if you incorporate your business with modern technology, such eatOS POS system , which can make real-time decisions. It is easier to also get reports on sales data, refunds, voids, labor costs, across email, text, website, third-party software, or mobile app anywhere, anytime."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_e922ba9e9ceb4e928da15c69b9e438d6~mv2.jpg', 'Marketing & Loyalty', 'eatOS Staff', '2025-05-01', 'published'),
  ('invest-in-food-franchises-unlock-the-latest-industry-trends-with-2023-insights', 'Invest in Food Franchises: Unlock the latest Industry trends', 'Check out some anticipated developments for the restaurant business in 2023. The food sector is your next greatest investment, according to We Sell Restaurants, which examines numerous franchise models and the most...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Check out some anticipated developments for the restaurant business in 2023. The food sector is your next greatest investment, according to We Sell Restaurants, which examines numerous franchise models and the most recent restaurant market trends."},{"type":"h2","text":"Delicious ideas for the future: The 2023 Restaurant Industry Outlook"},{"type":"p","text":"The pandemic epidemic forced the food service sector to reconsider its conventional operating procedures. To maintain sales, restaurant owners had to close dining rooms, lay off personnel, and reduce menu items. They relied on curbside pickup, deliveries, and government bailouts to keep in business. The National Restaurant Association estimates that at least 90,000 restaurants have closed permanently or for an extended period because of the outbreak, according to the National Restaurant Association."},{"type":"p","text":"This winter, the incidence of COVID, the flu, and RSV is rising, but the pandemic''s effects on the restaurant business are dissipating. The broad availability of vaccines and the relaxation of the mask regulations has revitalized the sector. Restaurant sales are increasing, and patrons are returning to indoor dining."},{"type":"p","text":"Despite higher menu pricing and growing inflation, the restaurant business is in good shape. The National Restaurant Association predicted that in 2022, the food service sector would generate $898 billion (about $2,800 per person in the US) (about $2,800 per person in the US). The National Restaurant Association reported that restaurants and bars added a net 62,100 jobs in November, marking the 23rd consecutive month of job growth, despite warnings from analysts about an impending recession and consumers cutting back on their spending. Staffing levels are still below their pre-pandemic levels despite the industry reporting growth. Other difficulties are emerging as the pandemic threat diminishes. High food prices, labor shortages, and soaring inflation significantly impact the business. To improve their profit line, operators reduced menu options and boosted pricing."},{"type":"h2","text":"Restaurant Trends for 2023"},{"type":"p","text":"Innovations in technology and service are driven by the pandemic''s effects and consumer preferences to boost sales and fill job gaps. The food franchise industry is also forced to concentrate on adaptive growth as they expand or resell due to the expensive and scarce real estate supply."},{"type":"p","text":"Meal preparation: People depend on restaurants to take the strain out of mealtimes because they want help in the kitchen. According to the National Restaurant Association, at least 70% of Generation Z and Millennials use more restaurant-prepared foods in their home meals. A Reuben Package is available at the renowned Katz''s Delicatessen, which includes two pounds of sliced pastrami, rye bread, pickles, Russian dressing, and sauerkraut. Take-and-bake pizzas are available from California Pizza Kitchen, and a DIY at-home pretzel kit is available from Auntie Ann''s."},{"type":"p","text":"Subscription services: Given the availability of subscription services for anything from dog food to cleaning supplies, it is expected that restaurants are now considering the advantages of providing pre-paid meal plans. One of the most recent and profitable developments in the restaurant business is meal subscriptions, which help businesses develop a network of devoted patrons."},{"type":"p","text":"Self-service: The restaurant sector is accelerating the implementation of new technology to improve service due to the pandemic, a labor shortage, and consumer preferences. Numerous chains are introducing contactless service options. Younger generations favor contactless services because of their convenience. Even quick-service restaurants like Chipotle and McDonald''s are implementing contactless drive-thru ordering lanes at certain locations."},{"type":"p","text":"Automation: To deal with labor constraints, restaurant industry trends show that restaurants are turning to technology to help streamline back-of-the-house processes. Using robots to flip burgers or slice veggies can free up employees to serve clients while improving consistency."},{"type":"p","text":"Loyalty programs: Loyalty programs are becoming increasingly popular as customers look for methods to save money. Offering discounts and incentives to regular customers is a simple approach for restaurants to increase repeat business. When advertising budgets are tight, this is a cost-effective marketing tactic."},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on carbon footprint: As environmental awareness grows, operators will do their share to provide sustainable packaging and reduce trash. Many restaurants have gone digital to cut expenses and minimize the inconvenience of updating menu boards when they make changes."},{"type":"h2","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"While the restaurant business has been slower to embrace technology than others, things are changing because of the pandemic and its effects. Calling restaurants is out; booking a table online is in - and digital platforms like products of eatO S are opening new opportunities to the food industry. QR codes are also here to stay, allowing access to online menus as well as an easy way to pay."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_c47596806bd841a0b89d4f7e98a56129~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Growth', 'eatOS Staff', '2025-04-29', 'published');
